# Testing Rules (WatchAgent)

- Tests must never call the real Open-Meteo API; weather-client calls are mocked/stubbed.
- Event detection tests must include both triggering and non-triggering examples for each signal to control false positives.
- API tests must assert response structure and ordering semantics (for example most-recent-first), not only HTTP status codes.
- Use isolated temporary SQLite databases for tests that touch persistence logic.
- Poller tests should mock the weather client so poller behavior is tested independently of network conditions.
- When a Cursor skill is a graded deliverable, add at least one focused test for its core behavior rather than treating it as untested tooling.
